    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d560">

                <pb facs="0678" n="618" xml:id="pg618"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Sir
                            Julian Pauncefote</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-13"><hi rendition="#italic">May 13,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 101.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to state that the
                    revenue-cutter <hi rendition="#italic">Perry</hi> intends to sail from San
                    Francisco for Bering Sea on to-morrow; the 14th instant, and to inquire whether
                    you have received the names of the British vessels, with their officers, spoken
                    of in my note of the 7th instant. In case you have not yet received the desired
                    information, I shall very greatly appreciate your courtesy in telegraphing for
                    it, so that this Government may be apprised thereof to-day or at the earliest
                    possible moment.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
